; lang.xon -- what this bundle IS.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every other
; manifest in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon).  A form a reader
; does not know is a loud error, never a skip -- a manifest that silently
; ignores half of itself cannot be extended without wondering which readers
; obeyed which half.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a REQUIREMENT, not a taste
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (requires-lang "NAME")      another lang this one is written on top of
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "r7rs")

; XENON, for the same reason x-r5rs is: Scheme's numerics are the tower.  Not
; radon, because the two modules that wanted dlopen -- x/bytevector.x and
; scm/ports.scm -- are not loaded in this release.
(dialect xe)

; PAIRING, NOT PINNING.  A digest freezes bytes; it says nothing about whether
; those bytes still run against a platform that moved.  This row is the part
; that is checkable, and it is compared for EQUALITY, never parsed.
;
; v0.6.0 is the first release carrying what this bundle needs: bundle
; acquisition, `-l` loading, --share-dir answering from any cwd, and eval! in
; the seam.  It is also what these specs are green against.

(requires-release "v0.6.0")

; R7RS IS R5RS PLUS about 700 lines, and this row is what says so.
;
; x.sh resolves it the same way it resolves -l, arms the required lang's root
; BEFORE this bundle's own (import-path! prepends, so ours still wins any name
; we share), and refuses at startup naming what is missing and who asked for it.
;
; Before the row existed the dependency lived as a probe in run.x: derive our
; own root, look beside it for r5rs/ or x-r5rs/, and hope.  That made a missing
; lang a runtime message rather than a refusal, recorded nothing about WHAT was
; needed, and would have been re-derived by every dependent.  The same argument
; (dialect ...) already makes -- a requirement belongs in the manifest.
;
; No version here, deliberately: lang.xon has no row for a bundle's OWN
; version, so there is nothing for a constraint to compare against.  Which
; release you get is lang.pin.xon's question, and it answers it with a digest.
(requires-lang "r5rs")

(entry "run.x")
